type: software
title: "How a reversible transition amplifies apparent entropy production"
abstract: "Unrefereed research candidate. Harunari, Fiore and Barato proposed estimating the entropy production of a periodically driven system from waiting-time histograms recorded with the driving protocol and with the protocol reversed, without recording the phase. They proved that the estimate minus a correction X is a lower bound and left open whether the uncorrected estimate is one. It is not, and its excess is unbounded: in a three-state model with zero period-averaged currents and fixed entropy production 4 pi/5, the estimate grows linearly with the rate of a reversible transition; exact rational certificates give more than 31 and, with lag bins, more than 145 times the entropy production. For any finite driven network, blocks of m waits overshoot the phase-resolved bound by at most X/m, and the coefficient cannot be lowered. Harunari, Fiore and Barato's corrected inequality remains valid."
